From 77c87c7a874db04ce0048719e2fc4172143f7521 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auditor <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:28:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] broker/persistence: recover landed orders, chase
 'unknown' rows, refuse on venue-only positions

INVARIANT PROTECTED: the ledger never knows LESS than the venue about a
position that can lose money. Where it cannot know, the process refuses
to trade rather than trading blind.

Findings (audit S2, S3, S7 - all rated HIGH):
  S2  POST /v5/order/create retried after a transport timeout whose first
      attempt landed. The retry is rejected as a duplicate orderLinkId
      (not in TRANSIENT_RET_CODES) -> PermanentAPIError -> _submit wrote
      the local row 'rejected' although the order EXISTS at the venue.
      The engine then reported REJECTED, placed no stop, recorded no
      position. Health stayed green. A naked live position, invisible.
  S3  An exhausted retry loop wrote status 'unknown' with the comment
      "leave the intent pending so reconciliation resolves it" - but
      pending_orders() selects only pending/submitted/partial, so
      'unknown' rows were never revisited by anything.
  S7  reconcile_on_startup walked the LEDGER only. It never read
      /v5/position/list, so a position the ledger never recorded (S2/S3
      aftermath, a manual trade) was invisible for the life of the
      process.

Thought process: three separate fixes, each the smallest one that fails
closed. (1) A duplicate-id rejection is evidence the order exists: ask
get_order() and record the exchange's answer; never resubmit; if the
lookup itself fails or returns nothing, leave 'unknown' so (2) picks it
up. (2) Add unresolved_orders() = pending + 'unknown', used by startup
reconciliation ONLY - pending_orders() is deliberately untouched because
shutdown() cancels through it and must never try to cancel an order the
venue may never have received. (3) For linear, read the venue position
per configured symbol; any position the ledger does not know is reported
as orphan_positions and main.startup() refuses to start. The process does
not try to adopt or close it: that is a human decision at a $100 cap and
a catastrophic automation at any bigger one.

What changed:
  bybit_connection.py - DUPLICATE_LINK_ID_RET_CODES {110072 linear, 170130
        spot}; _looks_like_duplicate_link_id (code OR message);
        _recover_landed_order; reconcile_on_startup(symbols=) with
        venue position check on linear; summary gains orphan_positions.
  persistence.py      - StateStore.unresolved_orders()
  trading_engine.py   - reconcile() passes cfg.TRADING_SYMBOLS
  main.py             - startup refuses on orphan_positions
  tests/test_reconcile_orphans_and_duplicates.py - 6 tests incl. a lossy
        transport that drops the create reply after the fake accepted it;
        asserts exactly one venue order and a truthful local row.

CANNOT DETERMINE without a venue: whether 110072 is the exact code every
Bybit linear account returns today (the message match is the backstop),
and the /v5/position/list shape for hedge-mode accounts (this client
sends positionIdx=0 and does not support hedge mode).

Verification: new tests 6/6 fail on baseline, pass after. 299 passed
across bybit_connection, orchestrator, paper cert and the two new files.
